  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As a content creator, I share my PoV to my viewers and the file location of photos is OPENLY VISIBLE in the camera menu.  The file location contains a portion of my real name, which I would not like to share to public.  I have streamed VRChat for years without issues and this only became a problem in the last few months.  Turning on Streamer Mode hides this, but Streamer Mode is very restrictive and does not work well with some settings (such as chat box) or when you are with your community or friends.  At the very least, please hide the file location to like the expanded settings menu or make it so it is visible on click.\n\nTLDR: Hide file location for camera quick menu to either expanded settings or revealed when clicked as it currently doxxes content creators sharing PoV in non-streamer mode.\n\nThank you\n\nAs of VRChat 2025.1.1 build 1567 on Jan. 29, this has been resolved with the following line on patch note:\n\n\"Your local display path will no longer be visible when using the Camera.\"\n\nIt has been switched to a button.\n\nThank you everyone!",
